        <!-- Authentication -->
        <section id="authentication" class="docs-section">
          <h2 class="docs-h2">Authentication</h2>
          <p class="docs-p">In <strong>development</strong>, pass the dev header to simulate a user:</p>
          <div class="docs-codeblock">
            <div class="docs-codeblock-header">
              <span>HTTP header</span>
            </div>
            <pre><code>x-dev-user-id: dev-user-1</code></pre>
          </div>
          <p class="docs-p">The dashboard sends this header automatically in development mode. In production, replace the auth middleware in <code class="docs-code">apps/api/src/middleware/index.ts</code> with your auth provider (JWT, session cookies, etc.).</p>
        </section>

        <!-- Production Deploy -->
        <section id="deploy-production" class="docs-section">
          <h2 class="docs-h2">Production deploy</h2>

          <h3 class="docs-h3">1. Set secrets</h3>
          <div class="docs-codeblock">
            <div class="docs-codeblock-header">
              <span>terminal</span>
            </div>
            <pre><code><span class="text-[#7c8594]"># Set each secret on Cloudflare</span>
wrangler secret put OPENHANDLE_LIVE_KEY
wrangler secret put OPENHANDLE_TEST_KEY
wrangler secret put META_APP_ID
wrangler secret put META_APP_SECRET
wrangler secret put META_REDIRECT_URI</code></pre>
          </div>

          <h3 class="docs-h3">2. Apply migrations to production D1</h3>
          <div class="docs-codeblock">
            <div class="docs-codeblock-header">
              <span>terminal</span>
            </div>
            <pre><code>pnpm --filter @instagram-widget/api exec wrangler d1 execute \
  instagram-widget-db \
  --file=../../database/migrations/0000_bouncy_peter_parker.sql

pnpm --filter @instagram-widget/api exec wrangler d1 execute \
  instagram-widget-db \
  --file=../../database/migrations/0001_old_risque.sql</code></pre>
          </div>

          <h3 class="docs-h3">3. Deploy the API worker</h3>
          <div class="docs-codeblock">
            <div class="docs-codeblock-header">
              <span>terminal</span>
            </div>
            <pre><code>pnpm --filter @instagram-widget/api exec wrangler deploy</code></pre>
          </div>

          <h3 class="docs-h3">4. Build static apps</h3>
          <div class="docs-codeblock">
            <div class="docs-codeblock-header">
              <span>terminal</span>
            </div>
            <pre><code><span class="text-[#7c8594]"># Build everything</span>
pnpm build

<span class="text-[#7c8594]"># Or individually</span>
pnpm build:dashboard   <span class="text-[#7c8594]"># → apps/dashboard/dist/</span>
pnpm build:widget      <span class="text-[#7c8594]"># → apps/widget/dist/</span>
pnpm build:web         <span class="text-[#7c8594]"># → apps/web/dist/</span></code></pre>
          </div>
          <p class="docs-p">Deploy the dashboard and widget <code class="docs-code">dist/</code> folders to any static host: Cloudflare Pages, Vercel, Netlify, or a CDN.</p>

          <h3 class="docs-h3">5. Cron triggers</h3>
          <p class="docs-p">The API worker includes a cron trigger configured to run every 6 hours (<code class="docs-code">0 */6 * * *</code>). This is defined in <code class="docs-code">wrangler.jsonc</code> and activates automatically on deploy. It refreshes feed data from OpenHandle so widgets stay up-to-date without manual intervention.</p>
        </section>

